5. Validation Against Existing Literature

Our framework integrates and extends several established research directions.

Reversal Curse (Berglund et al., 2023). We provide a categorical origin: the absence of an Inversion Functor. This moves the phenomenon from an empirical limitation to a structural necessity, proving that scaling alone cannot resolve it.

Directional Sensitivity in LLMs. Recent studies show LLMs encode narrative direction and perform better on forward predictions. Our metric descent condition gives a precise tool to measure directional asymmetry at the level of atomic arithmetic operations.

Recursive Intelligence (SRI) and Stability Toolkits. Our refined Stability Index with KL-divergence contributes a measurable, optimizable metric for thought-action alignment, essential for any recursive self-improving system.

Bounded-Uncertainty Decision Theory (BUDT). The potential energy model and the activation energy W_{\text{reason}} embody the BUDT principle that uncertainty should be actively managed rather than eliminated. The CIVT theorem provides a direct stress test for BUDT‑compliant agents.

